    <string name="notif_last_chance_title">Last chance: %1$s</string>
    <string name="notif_last_chance_text">A wished game, free on %1$s, not claimed yet: %2$s left.</string>
    <string name="set_last_chance">Last-chance alarm</string>
    <string name="last_chance_title">Last-chance alarm</string>
    <string name="last_chance_text">When a game from your wishlist is free and ends in under 3 hours without being yours (a captcha, a lost session, a store the app cannot claim), the phone rings like an alarm clock, even in silent mode, until you tap or dismiss it. It rings between 3 and 2 hours before the end: Android does not guarantee the minute to apps that are not alarm clocks. Opening the app silences it. You can change its sound or let it through Do Not Disturb in the channel settings.</string>
