    <string name="health_guide_intro">Steps for your phone (%1$s). Menu names vary.</string>
    <string name="health_battery_open">Open battery settings</string>
    <string name="guide_oplus">1. Settings › Battery (or Apps › App management) › Free Games Claimer › allow background activity, and turn on « Allow auto-launch ».\n2. In the recent apps list, lock the app (menu of its card › Lock) so « clear all » spares it.\n3. Do not swipe the app away to close it: on this system that stops it, and its alarms with it.</string>
    <string name="guide_xiaomi">1. Settings › Apps › Manage apps › Free Games Claimer › turn on « Autostart ».\n2. Same screen › Battery saver › « No restrictions ».\n3. In the recent apps list, lock the app (long press its card › lock icon).</string>
    <string name="guide_samsung">1. Settings › Battery › Background usage limits › Never sleeping apps › add Free Games Claimer.\n2. Settings › Apps › Free Games Claimer › Battery › « Unrestricted ».</string>
    <string name="guide_huawei">1. Settings › Battery › App launch › Free Games Claimer › switch to « Manage manually ».\n2. Turn on « Auto-launch », « Secondary launch » and « Run in background ».</string>
    <string name="guide_google">Settings › Apps › Free Games Claimer › App battery usage › « Unrestricted ». Pixel phones do not stop the app otherwise.</string>
    <string name="guide_other">Settings › Apps › Free Games Claimer › Battery: choose « Unrestricted » (or « Don\'t optimise »). If your phone has « Autostart » or « Background activity » options, turn them on, and lock the app in the recent apps list if it offers that.</string>
